.TH MAN 1 "FUZIX" "Ripple"
.SH NAME
man \- read command manuals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
man [-wqlv] [section] page
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Search /usr/man for a manual and format it with the built-in small man
formatter. Interactive output goes through more; Space advances, Enter
shows one line, and q quits. Redirected output is written directly.
.PP
-w prints the first matching pathname. -l reads a local file. -q suppresses
unknown formatter-command messages; -v enables them. A section restricts
the search, for example man 6 wump. Plain man and preformatted cat pages
are supported; compressed files and full groff/mdoc formatting are not.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
MANPATH is a colon-separated list of manual trees. MANSECT controls section
order; the default starts with 1, 6 and 8. PAGER selects the interactive
pager, including shell arguments, for example PAGER='less'.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
man intro
man sh
man 6 wump
man -w cp
man -l ./notes.1
man cp | col -b > cp.txt
.fi
